## Summary

I implemented **`TimelinePage`** — a native SwiftUI/HIG parity of the web `TimelinePage` (route `/timeline`) — adaptive across macOS + iOS, in `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Analytics/`.

**Delivered (all 35 parity items):**
- **7 panels:** 4 metric cards (Total Transitions / Driving / Charging / Idle-Sleep time), State Distribution bar + 8-state legend, Daily Breakdown panel, State Transitions table
- **1 chart:** stacked Daily Breakdown `BarChart` via the P3 `TSBarChart` Swift Charts wrapper (never a WKWebView)
- **4 data states:** loading / empty / error / success, each via shared components
- **23 required strings** (+ 11 nav/chrome) in `Localizable.xcstrings`, web key names preserved
- `@Observable TimelinePageModel` over a `TimelineDataSource` seam (ADR-004, no networking in the view); SI seconds formatted at the render boundary; new `.timeline` route wired into the shell + deep-link parser.

**Verification (in-scope gates all GREEN):**
